@ 23936 start
@ 23936 org
w 23936 Dictionary index: where each letter's words start
D 23936 32 two-byte offsets from #R$5DBE($5DBF). Entries 1-26 (indexed by a letter's ASCII code AND $1F) give the first word starting with that letter; entry 31 marks the end of the dictionary (#R$67B7). The tokenizer (#R$DA34) finds the end of a letter's words by skipping forward to the next non-zero entry.
D 23936 CORRECTED: the automatic code/data split had this as code, which is why it used to disassemble as nonsense.
