b 24000 The dictionary: 592 words
D 24000 Each record (see dictionary.py, which decodes them exactly as #R$A94D does): byte 0's low nibble picks a suffix from the table at #R$A85C ($F = none); byte 1 says how many characters to keep from the previous word (bits 4-6) and how many new 5-bit letters follow (bits 0-3); if bit 7 of byte 1 is set, two more bytes give the offset of the word this one is a synonym of. The first letter is never stored: it is implied by the letter index.
D 24000 Because each word is stored as a change to the previous one, words can only be decoded in order - the reason a standalone call to #R$A94D early in this project produced garbage.
D 24000 Checked against play: every word the game accepted or echoed decodes correctly, and the synonym links match its behaviour (READ is EXAMINE: READ CHRONICLE answers '...THAT YOU CAN EXAMINE'; PICK is CARRY: PICK UP LAMP answers 'I DO NOT KNOW THE VERB UP CARRY'; BREAK is KILL). One link is unexplained: IN is recorded as a synonym of VISITED.
