b 34017 Room records (rooms 0-105)
D 34017 Layout (see rooms.py, which decodes it the way the code reads it): byte 0 flags; +1..+6 up to three word slots naming the room - noun first, its top nibble the article (1 'a', 2 'an', 8 none); +7/+8 the room's own description message (0 = none); then exits, 3 bytes each - direction (the verb number 1-10), the thing in the way (0 = nothing) and the destination room - ended by $FF.
D 34017 The thing in the way is what the room description names: "To the east there is a deep stream" comes from an exit whose 'door' is the stream. An exit with destination 0 is only ever scenery: the exit finder #R$D448 skips it, so it is described but never offered as a visible exit and can't be taken.
D 34017 Confirmed by play: all 206 exits were tried (tools/walkall.py); 194 move the player to the decoded destination, and the other 12 are exactly the ones the code says must refuse - 7 scenery exits with destination 0, and 5 through a passage narrower than the player (see the move pre-check at #R$DCD2).
