b 39549 Three bytes ($FF, 0, 0) referenced from $BD4D
D 39549 Addresses named in the title: #R$BD4B($BD4D).
c 39550 Action record: default for verb 32 (HELLO)
D 39550 The record is only its two header bytes: HELLO has no body of its own, and the code that follows at #R$9A80 is what runs. Played: HELLO by itself prints 'HI.' and takes no time; SAY TO WATSON "HELLO" makes Watson answer 'Watson says " Good morning "'. In the stored routes this body ran 11 times, all with Chief Constable Straker as the actor.
B 39550,2 Action record header: flags $00; byte 1 $00
c 39552 Print one of two messages, depending on who is acting
D 39552 Referenced from #R$F725. If the actor (#R$A032($A036)) is you, prints #R$6915 and stores 1 at #R$A022($A027); otherwise prints #R$6920 and stores 0. Returns NZ (success). Read from code.
R 39552 Output:F NZ (success)
R 39552 $A027 1 if the actor is you, 0 if someone else
C 39552 The actor
C 39555 Compare A with $00 - You?
C 39557 Load A with $01
C 39559 Point HL at the message "HI." (#R$6915)
C 39562 If A equals $00, skip ahead to #R$9A90
C 39564 Someone else
C 39565 Point HL at the message "YOU SAY" GOOD MORNING "." (#R$6920)
C 39568 Store A in #R$A022($A027) in "Game variables"
C 39571 Print it
C 39574 Make A non-zero, which clears the zero flag, and hand that back to the caller - Succeed
C 39576 Return to the caller
c 39577 Shared action 1: the police cab, GO TO (Leatherhead routes, $9AA3)
D 39577 Addresses named in the title: #R$9AA3.
D 39577 Header $04 $00 then code. #R$9AA3 knows the police cab's only three routes, from the room it is in (#R$A00A) to the direct object: Old Mill Road to Main Street (L = 112), Main Street to Old Mill Road (114) and Main Street to Kings Cross Road (94); anything else refuses (#R$DC15). L becomes the journey's length (#R$A01A($A01F), at #R$9B04), the vehicle to move is the police cab (thing 109 = $6D, put in #R$E2C6), and the ride ends at #R$9B20 by handing back the vehicle sub-script #R$F3AD.
D 39577 Confirmed in the emulator (tools/experiments/chase.py stage P): told SAY TO POLICE MAN "GO TO KINGS CROSS ROAD" in Leatherhead's Main Street at 5:07pm, the police cab - with Lestrade and Watson aboard - reached Kings Cross Road at 6:42, 95 minutes. Asked for Buckingham Palace Road it did nothing. CORRECTED: was data in the automatic split.
R 39577 Input:IX The action record
R 39577 Output:F Z when the route is refused; otherwise continues at $9AD7
B 39577,2 Action record header: flags $04; byte 1 $00
