b 39807 Cab journeys: which cab stands a hansom cab runs between, and how long it takes
D 39807 Three-byte entries (one stand, the other stand, a number), ended by $FF, searched either way round by #R$9C07. The ten stands are street rooms: Portman, Baker, Parliament, Slater, Aldergate and Sidmouth Streets, Kings Cross Road, Bishops Road, Buckingham Palace Road and Camden Street; every pair of them has an entry (45 entries). The third byte is the journey's length in minutes: the cab-ride action record at #R$9AE3 puts it, less 2, in #R$A01A($A01F), the number of minutes an action takes; and Parliament Street to Kings Cross Road, 12 here, matches Lestrade's cab ride logged in the emulator (7:10 to 7:20am). #R$9B25 also prices the ride from it. Leatherhead and Old Mill Road are not here: they are reached by train and the police cab.
D 39807 Confirmed in the emulator (tools/experiments/cab_test.py): hailed in Baker Street, the cab took 19-20 minutes to Parliament Street (the table says 20), and the cabbie then said 'Right guv'nor that will be 10d.'; asked for Old Mill Road, which is not in the table, he replied 'Sorry guv'nor I cannot get there from'ere'.
