C 40742 ...and held by nothing (+1 = $FF)
C 40746 Read byte +6 of the record at IY into L - The actor's next turn (IY+6/+7) is DE minutes later
C 40749 Read byte +7 of the record at IY into H
C 40752 Add DE to HL
C 40753 Store L in byte +6 of the record at IY
C 40756 Store H in byte +7 of the record at IY
C 40759 Return to the caller
b 40760 Each verb's default action record
D 40760 Three-byte records (verb number, address of an action record), ended by $FF, searched by #R$D34E from #R$C972. 38 of the 54 verbs have a default here; several verbs share one record (all ten directions use #R$DD03; TAKE, GET, CARRY, TAKE FROM and TAKE OUT OF all use #R$DCC1; PUT IN, PUT ON and DROP IN use #R$DEC1).
D 40760 Verbs with no entry here (CLIMB INTO, CLIMB OUT OF, CLOSE, COUNT, GET INTO, GET OUT OF, GO TO, HAIL, OPEN, SIT IN, TAKE OFF, TAKE TO, WEAR, LOCK, UNLOCK) do nothing unless the object itself lists the verb in its own action list - which is why OPEN only ever reached a door's own entry.
D 40760 Confirmed by breakpointing #R$C972/#R$C981 during real commands and logging the verb and the record found (LOOK 34 -> #R$DC7B, INVENTORY 33 -> #R$DE6F, TAKE 41 -> #R$DCC1, DROP 16 -> #R$DC8D, WAIT 49 -> #R$DDB4).
