C 41090 Test bit 7 of A
C 41092 If bit 7 of A is clear, skip ahead to #R$A093
C 41094 Compare A with $8D - ...and is it ENTER?
C 41096 If A differs from $8D, skip ahead to #R$A093
C 41098 Read minutes since the start (#R$9FDD) into HL - Then the player acts now: next-turn time = this minute
C 41101 Store L in byte +6 of the record at IY
C 41104 Store H in byte +7 of the record at IY
C 41107 Walk the actor table
C 41111 Read the first byte of the record at IY into A - End of the table?
C 41114 Add one to A
C 41115 Yes: the next minute
C 41117 Read minutes since the start (#R$9FDD) into HL - Has this actor's time come?
C 41120 Call #R$A0DB (inside "The main loop: one minute of game time per...")
C 41123 Not yet: next actor
C 41125 Read the first byte of the record at IY into A - Start its turn
C 41128 Save IY on the stack
C 41130 Save AF on the stack
C 41131 Call the routine "Start an actor's turn" (#R$CC37)
C 41134 Restore AF from the stack - One plan step
C 41135 Save AF on the stack
C 41136 Call the routine "Run one step of the current actor's plan script" (#R$CC78)
C 41139 Read #R$A01A($A01F) in "Game variables" into HL - Did it take any time?
C 41142 Copy L into A
C 41143 Set in A the bits that are set in H
C 41144 If the result is zero, go back to #R$A0AE - No: another step
C 41146 Restore AF from the stack
C 41147 Restore IY from the stack
