c 41415 Free node IX back to the heap
D 41415 Puts the block back in the free list in address order and joins it to free neighbours (#R$A20C).
D 41415 How it works:
D 41415 1. Save HL and DE, and work out where the freed block starts: three bytes before the node in IX.
D 41415 2. Walk the list of free blocks from its head at #R$9FE3. The list is kept in address order, so stop at the first free block that lies above this one, or at the end of the list.
D 41415 3. Link the block in at that point: the previous link now points at it, and its own link points at the block that came after.
D 41415 4. Try to join it to the free block that follows it (#R$A20C). If the freed block joined onto the one before it instead, step back to that block and try again to join it to what follows.
R 41415 Input:IX The node to free
R 41415 IX is not preserved
