c 41484 Join free block IX to the next one if they touch
D 41484 Used by #R$A1C7. NZ if there is no next free block; Z after joining (sizes added, link taken over).
D 41484 How it works:
D 41484 1. Work out the address just past this free block: its start plus the size held in its first two bytes.
D 41484 2. Read the link to the next free block. If there is none, return NZ.
D 41484 3. If the next free block does not start at exactly that address, return NZ: there is a gap between them.
D 41484 4. Otherwise add the next block's size to this one's and take over the next block's link, which unhooks it from the list, and return Z.
R 41484 Input:IX The link field of a free block (its size is the word before it)
R 41484 Output:F Z if the next free block was joined on, NZ if not
