c 41853 Print the rest of a narrated command: verb words, objects, numbers
D 41853 Part of #R$A2E4. From the verb pattern (#R$A2B1/#R$A2BD) and the parse flags (#R$A01A($A01D)/#R$A01A($A01E)) prints the verb's words (#R$A880), then the direct object - as a number or money (#R$A419) when it is one ($FE), as ME (word $055B, looked up with source/dictionary.py; CORRECTED, was 'yourself') when it is the actor, or by name (#R$A745) - then any preposition and the indirect object the same way, and a full stop. Read from the code; 'You pay 2/6 to Watson.' in the emulator is one of its sentences.
D 41853 How it works:
D 41853 1. Look up the remembered command's verb record and flags (#R$A2B1, #R$A2BD, #R$C493, #R$C4B2).
D 41853 2. Print the verb's words: the pair at +6 of the record, then the pair at +0 (#R$A880).
D 41853 3. If the verb takes a direct object (flags bit 3): print any word that goes before it, then the object itself - a number or sum of money (#R$A419) if it is one, ME if it is the actor, or its name (#R$A745).
D 41853 4. If there is an indirect object and the flags allow one: print its preposition, then the object the same three ways.
D 41853 5. End with a full stop. The result is a sentence such as 'You pay 2/6 to Watson.'
R 41853 Input:$A35D The remembered command: verb, direct object, indirect object
