c 43136 Print the dictionary word that HL refers to
D 43136 HL points at a 2-byte word reference (low 12 bits: offset into the dictionary; high nibble: flags). Prints nothing when output is switched off (#LINK(rom_symbols#a5C3C)($5C3C) = 0: the text belongs to something the player cannot see) or the reference is 0. Otherwise prints a space, finds the word through the per-letter index at #R$5D80, prints it (#R$A95B) and its suffix. Called by the object-name printers at #R$A39E($A39F)-#R$A3F7($A3F8) and by #R$D5E4($D5E5). Read from the code, not traced in detail.
D 43136 .
D 43136 Line comments added from reading the code; the flag-nibble rule for the suffix ($50/$40/$10) is read from the branches, not yet shown by playing.
D 43136 How it works:
D 43136 1. Take the 12-bit offset and the flag nibble from the two bytes at HL; print nothing if output is off (#LINK(rom_symbols#a5C3C)($5C3C)) or the offset is 0.
D 43136 2. Print a space, then find the letter whose records contain the offset by searching the per-letter index at #R$5D80.
D 43136 3. From that letter's first record, spell each record (#R$A95B) until the offset is reached; the spelling is built at #LINK(rom_symbols#a5C42)($5C42) from its kept letters, new packed letters and suffix.
D 43136 4. Print the spelling a letter at a time through the word-wrap printer, applying capitals and the flag nibble's rules.
R 43136 Input:HL A word reference (two bytes)
R 43136 Output:HL Past the reference
R 43136 The word printed
