c 43540 Send one character to the screen layer
D 43540 Letters become lower case; a space at the start of a line is dropped; carriage returns, quote marks and full stops get special handling (the rest: a full stop or quote mark makes the next letter a capital, and #R$A851 makes them all capitals).
D 43540 How it works:
D 43540 1. A capital letter becomes lower case; everything else is passed on as it is.
D 43540 2. A space at the start of a line is dropped (#R$A022($A025) is zero until the first real character of the line).
D 43540 3. A carriage return starts a new line. A quote mark gets a space put in front of it. A quote mark or a full stop sets #R$A022($A026), so the next letter will be a capital.
D 43540 4. A lower-case letter becomes a capital if the all-capitals flag #R$A851 is set or #R$A022($A026) is set; #R$A022($A026) is cleared as it is used.
D 43540 5. Pass the character to the screen layer (#R$C1E1).
R 43540 Input:A The character
