w 43633 Shared action records, used through objects' own action lists
D 43633 24 addresses of action records, ended by $0000. An object's own action list (see the entity records at #R$8CBA) maps a verb number to an index here; #R$C960 looks the index up when the target object has an entry for the verb being carried out. That lets every door share one OPEN and one CLOSE, every chair one SIT IN, and so on.
D 43633 Which objects use which entries was read from all 110 entity records (objects.py); entries 1-3, 13-15 and 22 are not used by any object's action list and may be reached some other way - not yet found.
D 43633 CORRECTED HISTORY: this table was first taken for the verb dispatch table (wrong - see #R$9F38), then 'TAKE is entry 5' was claimed and withdrawn. Entry 5 is in fact TAKE OFF.
D 43633 People have action lists too, after a 00 entry in their records (see #R$C933): the local police man maps GO TO and GO FURIOUSLY TO to entries 1 and 2, the cabbies TAKE TO, GO TO and GO FURIOUSLY TO to 13, 14 and 15, Tricia Fender has entry 3 and Mrs Jones has entry 22 - which is how the entries no object uses are reached.
