c 44068 Read a noun phrase into the pattern at $AAA8
D 44068 Addresses named in the title: #R$AAA3($AAA8).
D 44068 Clears ten bytes at #R$AAA3($AAA8), then takes tokens: an article ($80) once; up to three of class $10 or $70 (prepositions; counted in #R$AAA3($AAA7), stored by #R$AC8F); adjectives ($60, by #R$AC94); and ends on the noun ($50) or a number ($F0), whose reference goes to #R$AAAB($AAAC). Carry when a word comes in the wrong place; on return NZ if bit 5 of E is set. Read from the code; the meaning of each E flag bit was not traced.
D 44068 Instruction coverage over the 15 stored routes (9 November, tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py): all 53 instructions were executed.
D 44068 How it works:
D 44068 1. Clear the ten bytes of the noun-phrase pattern at #R$AAA3($AAA8) and set E bits 2, 4 and 5.
D 44068 2. Take tokens. An article ($80) is allowed once, at the start; a second one returns carry.
D 44068 3. Up to three words of class $10 or $70 (adjectives and prepositions) are counted in #R$AAA3($AAA7) and stored by #R$AC8F or #R$AC94.
D 44068 4. A noun ends the phrase. The pattern is then copied into the node as the first or second object (#R$ACA6).
R 44068 Input:E Flags for the kinds of word still allowed (bits 2, 4, 5)
R 44068 Output:F Carry set for a word out of place
