D 44671 The word list built by #R$D715 (#LINK(rom_symbols#a5B81)($5B81) on) is a run of tokens: a class byte, then - for classes below $80 and for $90, $E0 and $F0 - a 2-byte word reference (high byte first) or value. Returns the class in A and D and the reference in BC, keeps the previous class at #R$A02A($A02D) and the token's address at #R$A022($A029).
D 44671 Confirmed in the emulator (tools/experiments/tokens_test.py): 'TAKE THE LAMP, EXAMINE IT. PAY 2/6 TO WATSON' becomes $30 TAKE, $80 (THE, no reference), $50 LAMP, $A0 (comma), $30 EXAMINE, $90 IT, $B0 (full stop), $30 PAY, $F0 #R$809A($809E) (2/6, 30 pence), $70 TO, $50 WATSON, $B0, $C0 (end). So $30 is a verb, $50 a noun, $70 a preposition, $80 a word with no meaning to the parser, $90 a special word (the table at #R$AF6B: IT, HE, QUIT, a quote mark...), $F0 a number or money, $A0 a comma, $B0 a full stop, $C0 the end. Other classes ($00, $20, $40, $E0, read by #R$AB91) were not seen in this line.
D 44671 How it works:
D 44671 1. Remember where the token starts (#R$A022($A029)) and the class of the one before (#R$A02A($A02D)).
D 44671 2. The class is the first byte. Classes $E0, $F0, $90 and those below $80 have a two-byte word after them, which is returned in BC.
D 44671 3. Save the position after the token and return the class in A.
R 44671 Input:D The previous class
R 44671 Output:A, D The class of the token
R 44671 BC The word reference (for classes with one)
R 44671 $A029 Where this token started
R 44671 $A02B The position after it
