c 45271 Load a saved game from tape
D 45271 Loads the game state (#R$B0EE: from #R$840B, 7,188 bytes, up to #R$A01A($A01F)) with the ROM's LD-BYTES (#R$C0DF), asking again until it loads, then restores IY from #R$9FD4 and returns to the main loop's restart at #R$A040. #R$B0E4 is the save: it keeps IY at #R$9FD4 and saves the same block (#R$C040). Read from the code; the harness cannot run the ROM's tape routines. Confirmed in the emulator only that a game over ends with 'PLAY SAVED GAME TAPE TO BE LOADED'.
