C 45291 Save it (and verify)
c 45294 The block a saved game holds: $840B up to $A01F
D 45294 Addresses named in the title: #R$840B, #R$A01A($A01F).
D 45294 IX = #R$840B (the room table), DE = #R$A01A($A01F) - #R$840B. So a saved game is the rooms, the entities, the case table, the actor table, the heap and the variables - but not the plan scripts, which never change (no script uses one-shot instructions).
