c 47210 Hand quoted words to the person spoken to (SAY TO / TALK TO)
D 47210 Called by the TALK TO body (#R$DDAE) with A = 1 if the person has a plan script (an actor, #R$CC0E) and 0 if not. Takes the next quoted sentence off the list at #R$9FEC. For an actor, #R$B8AA puts it on the order/remark list (#R$9FEE) as an 8-byte node: +0 the person, +1 0, +5/+6 the words, +7 = #R$A022($A024) (2 for a statement); the person deals with it on its next turn (#R$B936). For anyone else the words are just used up. Read from the code; the effect (Watson getting out of his chair, Watson and Lestrade answering statements) is confirmed in the emulator - see #R$CBA7, #R$BA67 and #R$BB67.
D 47210 CORRECTED: the automatic split had #R$B866-#R$B90D as data and text.
D 47210 How it works:
D 47210 1. Take the next quoted sentence from the list at #R$9FEC and unlink it.
D 47210 2. If the person has a plan script (A = 1), parse the words as a sentence of their own (#R$B8AA) and put them on the order and remark list at #R$9FEE as an 8-byte node.
D 47210 3. Otherwise skip the words to the end of the line and mark it with a $90 token.
R 47210 Input:A 1 if the person spoken to has a plan script; 0 if not
R 47210 Output:The quoted sentence handed over or used up
