c 47975 Lestrade's reply to something the player says
D 47975 Parses the remark into a statement the same way as Watson's reply (#R$BA67) and checks it against the case table: a statement whose evidence is complete is proven (#R$BCC9) and Lestrade says so; otherwise it is marked as waiting and he says he does not believe the player has the evidence (#R$72A6, #R$72BD).
D 47975 Confirmed in the emulator (see the case table at #R$9965): 'I do not believe that you have the evidence to prove that Mrs Brown killed herself' without the evidence, 'So Mrs Brown killed herself, excellent Holmes, another brilliant conclusion.' with it.
D 47975 Line comments added from reading the code and cover the first part only (to #R$BC0E); which exact reply each address holds was not rendered.
D 47975 Played, 9 November (a fresh replay of the winning route to Scotland Yard at 1:58pm on Tuesday, then sentences typed to Inspector Lestrade; the reply and the branch taken are given for each): MRS BROWN KILLED HERSELF - 'So Mrs Brown killed herself, excellent Holmes, another brilliant conclusion' (#R$BBE5, the statement is proven); MRS JONES KILLED TRICIA FENDER - 'Brilliant Holmes, I do not know how you do it' and Mrs Jones is led away; BASIL KILLED MRS BROWN, BASIL HAS THE PLANS and THE SALE LOCATION IS OLD MILL ROAD before the evidence is in - 'I do not believe that you have the evidence to prove that ...' (#R$BBC4, #R$72A6); TRICIA FENDER HAD PLANS - 'I do not see the importance of that'; BASIL KILLED WATSON, WATSON KILLED MRS BROWN, WHAT HAPPENED and THE PLANS ARE IN THE DRAWER - the stock reply 'That may well be, Holmes, I will think about it' (#R$BB87, #R$725F); a sentence with a word the game does not know is refused before it gets here (I DO NOT KNOW THE WORD). A plain HELLO does not come here at all: Lestrade answers 'Good afternoon' through #R$9A80.
D 47975 Branches reached later the same day (tools/experiments/tails_test.py to tails_test6.py, same set-up: the player put in Lestrade's room, then remarks typed): BASIL KILLED - a statement that stops after the verb - goes to #R$BBBE and Lestrade says 'What' (#R$7243). MAJOR FFOULKES VISITED THE OPIUM DEN with the Major's confession already poked in (bit 1 of #R$996F($9972)) and nothing else waiting goes through the summary at #R$BBC9, finds nothing unprovable and nothing newly provable (#R$BBD3), and Lestrade says 'Thats fine Holmes but what does it prove' (#R$727E at #R$BBDE). The same remark after TRICIA FENDER KILLED MRS JONES has been told (and left waiting) finds one newly provable statement (#R$BBD9): 'That is well and good, but I do not see how it proves that Tricia Fender killed Mrs Jones' (#R$72BD). After MAJOR FFOULKES IS INNOCENT is left waiting the same remark proves it and Lestrade says 'Very good Holmes, I shall return to Leather head tomorrow...', through #R$BBE5.
D 47975 Still not seen: #R$BBFB-#R$BC17, which names a statement with flags bit 4 that is still waiting. Only the four flags-$B4 statements (Tricia Fender or Phipps killed Mrs Brown or Mrs Jones) have that bit, and each has a child record that asks only that thing 0, the player, has been seen. They were always found provable, even in a run that cleared bit 7 of the player's +6 before the check (#R$BBD9 was taken instead), so no sentence that can be typed has been found to reach it, and I have not worked out why the poke made no difference. Those 12 of the routine's 93 instructions are read from the code; the other 81 have run, 66 of them in the stored routes.
