C 48205 Save HL on the stack
C 48206 Read the first byte of the record at IX into A - Walk the case table; $FF ends it
C 48209 Compare A with $FF
C 48211 If A equals $FF, skip ahead to #R$BC68
C 48213 Test bit 0 of byte +3 of the record at IX - Push each statement that is waiting (bit 0) and not of the bit-5 kind
C 48217 If bit 0 of byte +3 of the record at IX is clear, skip ahead to #R$BC63
C 48219 Test bit 5 of byte +3 of the record at IX
C 48223 If bit 5 of byte +3 of the record at IX is set, skip ahead to #R$BC63
C 48225 Save IX on the stack
C 48227 Call the routine "Step IX over one case record (4 bytes, or 6 with a..." (#R$BE5A) - Next statement (#R$BE5A)
C 48230 Go back to #R$BC4E
C 48232 Restore HL from the stack - Then pop them one by one and try to prove each (#R$BCC9)
C 48233 Copy H into A
C 48234 Set in A the bits that are set in L
C 48235 If the result is zero, return
C 48236 Save HL on the stack
C 48237 Restore IX from the stack
C 48239 Call the routine "Try to prove statement IX" (#R$BCC9)
C 48242 Go back to #R$BC68
