c 48465 Find the statement $BA19-$BA1B in the case table
D 48465 Addresses named in the title: #R$BA13($BA19), #R$BA1B.
D 48465 Z with IX = the statement if found (#R$BD69 compares subject, relation and object in that order). #R$BD4B searches Watson's own list at #R$9A7D the same way.
D 48465 How it works:
D 48465 1. Start at the first record of the case table (#R$9965), or - from #R$BD4B - at Watson's own list (#R$9A7D).
D 48465 2. A first byte of $FF ends the table: return NZ.
D 48465 3. Compare the record with the statement being looked for: its relation (#R$BA13($BA1A)) with byte +1, then its subject (#R$BA13($BA19)) with +0, then its object (#R$BA1B) with +2. All three must match.
D 48465 4. On a match return Z with IX at the record; otherwise step to the next record (#R$BE5A), skipping any evidence records that belong to this one, and repeat.
R 48465 Input:$BA19 The statement's subject
R 48465 $BA1A Its relation
R 48465 $BA1B Its object
R 48465 Output:F Z if found, NZ if not
R 48465 IX The record, if found
