c 48785 Check one piece of evidence (NZ if it holds)
D 48785 See the case table at #R$9965 for the four kinds. Marks it done (bit 1 set, bit 0 clear) when it holds.
D 48785 How it works:
D 48785 1. If the evidence is already marked done (bit 1 of its flags), it holds: finish.
D 48785 2. The top two bits of the flags give the kind. Kind 0: both things named in the record must have been seen by the player (bit 7 of their +6 flags); if so it holds. Kind $80 is a marker that only some other routine can set, so it never holds by itself.
D 48785 3. Kind $40: both things must have been examined (bit 6 of +6). Then, as for kind $C0 (which has no test of its own), it holds only if it has no children, or if all of its children hold (#R$BF08).
D 48785 4. When it holds, mark it done (bit 1 set, bit 0 clear) and return NZ.
R 48785 Input:IX An evidence record in the case table
R 48785 Output:F NZ if it holds, Z if not
