c 48924 Print a case statement: thing, relation, thing
D 48924 IX is a statement record of the case table (#R$9965): prints the first thing's name (#R$A4BC, #R$D3E8), the relation's verb words from the table at #R$994D (#R$BF45; relation 0 prints AND), then the second thing. Used by message code $05 (#R$A711). Read from the code; the output is what Lestrade says when a statement is waiting.
R 48924 Input:IX A statement record of the case table
R 48924 Output:The statement printed: thing, relation, thing
C 48924 Read the first byte of the record at IX into A - The statement's subject: thing +0 ... its name words (#R$A4BC, +7)
