b 49406 The saved game's tape header: a CODE file 'SHD V2.0'
D 49406 The standard 17-byte header SA-BYTES writes first: type 3 (code), the ten-letter name 'SHD V2.0  ', then the length, start and second parameter. The length and start words are where #R$C046/#R$C04A and #R$C0DF keep DE and IX between the header and the block, so they are filled in when the game is saved. A load reads a header into the same place. The original tape carries a block with this very name and range (#R$840B-#R$A01A($A01F), the saved-game block of #R$B0EE) - apparently a saved game, loaded before the main block and overwritten by it (see loader_notes.md). Read from the code.
