D 49449 Called at #R$A284, after the 18 newlines that clear the text window and before the room's picture is drawn in the top right quarter (#R$F3C2). Sets #R$C128, the characters-left count (#R$C1F5) to 18, the print position to $5020 and the pixel shift to 2, and clears the page line count (#R$A012($A019)). From then on the scroll (#R$C316) moves only the left 16 bytes of each pixel line and leaves the colours alone, so the picture stays where it is while the text runs beside it.
D 49449 CORRECTED 2026-11-08: the 18 was read as a number of lines. Confirmed in the emulator: in room 6 the description comes out 18 characters to a line ('You are in an | entrance hallway. | Above there is the | stairway...').
