c 49926 Page-wait: flash the cursor, wait for a key, clear
D 49926 Called by the character printer (#R$C2D1) when a newline comes after fifteen lines of text (#R$A012($A019) = 15) since the player last typed a command or pressed a key. Sets FLASH on the attribute at $5A5F - the right-hand end of the chain strip on row 18 - waits for a key via the GET-KEY wrapper at #R$C415, turns FLASH off again and makes the text lines full width (#R$C142). Nothing is cleared: the text simply carries on scrolling.
D 49926 Confirmed in the emulator 2026-11-08: typing LOOK. LOOK in the sitting room stops here with #R$A012($A019) = 15 part way through the second description, waiting for a key. CORRECTED: this was said to be triggered by #R$C1F5 (the characters left on the line) and to clear the screen.
R 49926 Output:A key waited for, the window cleared; HL kept
