C 49932 Block here until the player presses something
C 49935 Turn FLASH back off
C 49937 Clear the screen and reset the text window
C 49940 Restore HL
C 49941 Return to the caller
c 49942 Scroll the text up a line, printing the line that goes if printing is on
D 49942 Moves screen rows 1-17 up to rows 0-16, eight pixel lines at a time: all 32 bytes of each line in full-width mode, only the left 16 when a picture is showing (#R$C128 set). In full-width mode the colours of rows 1-17 move up too, and before anything moves the top row goes to the ZX Printer (#R$C3E4) if printing is on. Then row 17 is cleared with 36 (or 18) spaces. Called by the character printer at #R$C2DF on every newline. Read from the code; the narrow mode confirmed in the emulator (see #R$C129).
D 49942 How it works:
D 49942 1. At full width, send the top row to the printer (#R$C3E4) if printing is on.
D 49942 2. Move text rows 1 to 17 up to rows 0 to 16, eight pixel lines each, 32 bytes a line (16 beside a picture).
D 49942 3. Clear the bottom text row.
