c 50045 Swap DE and HL, then move HL down a character row
D 50045 Adds 32 to L, and 8 to H when that carries - the next character row, crossing into the next third of the screen when it has to. Because it swaps first, #R$C316 calls it twice to move both of its pointers on and leave them the right way round.
D 50045 CORRECTED 2026-11-08: this was described as the next pixel line; 32 bytes on in the Spectrum's screen is the next character row.
