C 50110 Shift the glyph byte left by that remaining amount...
C 50112 ...building a matching mask alongside it
C 50114 Shift B left, C times
C 50116 Subtract one from C
C 50117 If C is not zero, go back to #R$C3C0
C 50119 C = A; A = B complemented
C 50120 Copy B into A
C 50121 Flip every bit of A
C 50122 Move to the next screen byte along
C 50123 Clear the bits this glyph will occupy there...
C 50124 Set in A the bits that are set in C
C 50125 ...and merge the overflow bits in
C 50126 Move back (net: one screen byte to the right overall)
C 50127 Restore BC from the stack
C 50128 Step DE on to the next byte
C 50129 Next pixel row down
C 50130 Count B down and, while it is not zero, go back to #R$C39B
C 50132 Restore caller's registers
C 50133 Restore DE from the stack
C 50134 Restore BC from the stack
C 50135 C = the new column-shift for the next character:
