c 50179 Print one pixel line on the ZX Printer
D 50179 Port $FB is the ZX Printer's. Sets the printer speed (slower for the last two of the eight lines: the B < 3 test at #R$C403-#R$C407), waits until the printer is ready (IN A,($FB), RET M / JR NC) and joins the 48K ROM's COPY-LINE code at #LINK(rom_symbols#a0F12)($0F12), which prints one pixel line. Called eight times by #R$C3E4 for each character row sent to the printer, so it is reached only when printing is on (PRINT special word). CORRECTED: was 'Read a Kempston-style joystick port' - the Kempston joystick is port $1F; $FB with a jump into the ROM's COPY-LINE is the printer. Read from the code; not tried (no printer in the harness).
R 50179 Input:B The pixel line number
R 50179 HL The screen address of the line
R 50179 Output:The line sent to the printer through the ROM at $0F12
