c 50385 Carry out the command in $A033-$A035 for the current actor
D 50385 Addresses named in the title: #R$A032($A033), #R$A032($A035).
D 50385 The one entry point for doing a command, used for the player's typed commands and for every DO in a plan script. Verbs #R$E497(128) and up go to #R$C583 (the script-only verbs). Otherwise the requirement codes are set from the parse (#R$C493, #R$C4B2); when the verb needs an object but none was given (#R$A032($A034) = $FF), each candidate object (#R$C463) is tried in turn until one works (#R$C55A) - which is how a character's 'DO TAKE' with no object picks something up. Then #R$C929 finds and runs the action record. Read from the code.
D 50385 How it works:
D 50385 1. A verb number with bit 7 set is a script-only verb: use the numbered record (#R$C583).
D 50385 2. Otherwise find the verb's pattern record (#R$A2B1), gather its flags (#R$A2BD), and set the two objects' requirement codes (#R$C493, #R$C4B2).
D 50385 3. If a number is required, the object must be $FE. If a required direct object is still $FF, ask for it.
D 50385 4. Guess the indirect object when it is missing and the verb allows (#R$C542, #R$C55A), then check the record (#R$C929) and carry it out.
