c 50563 Pick one of the 13 numbered action records
D 50563 A = a record number with bit 7 set (a verb of 128 or more, from a DO in a plan script). Looks the record up in the table at #R$9FAB, then copies the low nibble of its byte 0 to #R$A00A($A00F) and of its byte 1 to #R$A00A($A010) (via #R$C571 and #R$C57A), and clears #R$A00A($A00B). Continues past this disassembly window - not traced further.
D 50563 .
D 50563 Line comments added from reading the code. CB41 is taken to be the "return Z" stub; the guessing loops only try candidates until the record runs, as the helpers at #R$C463/#R$C60D/#R$C613 describe.
D 50563 Instruction coverage over the 15 stored routes (9 November, tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py): 54 of 57 instructions executed; #R$C5C5 #R$C5C8 #R$C5CA never ran there and are read from the code only.
D 50563 How it works:
D 50563 1. The record number (bit 7 dropped) indexes the 13 record addresses at #R$9FAB.
D 50563 2. Set both requirement codes from the record's header (#R$C571, #R$C57A).
D 50563 3. If the record takes no objects, run it at once (#R$C5F4). If the direct object must be a number, #R$A032($A034) must be $FE or the command is refused.
D 50563 4. Guess a missing indirect object (#R$C60D) and run the record.
R 50563 Input:A A record number with bit 7 set
R 50563 Output:F Z if refused; NZ if the record ran
C 50563 Record number (bit 7 dropped) into DE
C 50565 Copy A into E
C 50566 Load D with $00
C 50568 Look it up in the table of 13 record addresses at #R$9FAB (2 bytes each)...
C 50571 Add DE to HL
C 50572 Add DE to HL
C 50573 ...
C 50574 Step HL on to the next byte
C 50575 Read the byte HL points at into D
C 50576 IX = HL = the record
C 50577 Save HL on the stack
C 50578 Restore IX from the stack
C 50580 #R$A00A($A00F) = requirement code of the direct object from the record's header (#R$C571)
C 50583 #R$A00A($A010) = the indirect object's (#R$C57A)
C 50586 #R$A00A($A00B) = 0
C 50587 Store A in #R$A00A($A00B) in "Game variables"
C 50590 Read #R$A00A($A00F) in "Game variables" into A - Both requirement codes zero (the record takes no objects)?
C 50593 Point HL at #R$A00A($A010) in "Game variables"
C 50596 Set in A the bits that are set in the byte at #R$A00A($A010) in "Game variables"
C 50597 Yes: run the record at once (#R$C5F4)
C 50599 Read #R$A00A($A00F) in "Game variables" into A - Direct object a number (code 5 or 6)?
C 50602 Compare A with $05
C 50604 If A equals $05, skip ahead to #R$C5B2
C 50606 Compare A with $06
C 50608 If A differs from $06, skip ahead to #R$C5BA
C 50610 Read #R$A032($A034) in "Game variables" into A - Then #R$A032($A034) must already hold $FE ('a number was given')...
C 50613 Compare A with $FE
C 50615 ...if not, give up: Z (#R$CB41)
C 50618 Read #R$A00A($A010) in "Game variables" into A - Same test for the indirect object and #R$A032($A035)
