C 51313 Load A with $FF
C 51315 Swap AF with the shadow copy
C 51316 Read byte +1 of the record at IX into A - Held by nothing ($FF): stop with A = the last holder
C 51319 Compare A with $FF
C 51321 If A equals $FF, skip ahead to #R$C895
C 51323 Swap AF with the shadow copy
C 51324 Read byte +1 of the record at IX into A - Otherwise A' = its holder, and IX = the holder's record (#R$D237)
C 51327 Call the routine "Resolve an id (in A) to its full entity record" (#R$D237)
C 51330 Test bit 7 of byte +5 of the record at IX - Keep climbing only if the holder has +5 bit 7 set...
C 51334 If bit 7 of byte +5 of the record at IX is clear, skip ahead to #R$C894
C 51336 Test bit 5 of byte +5 of the record at IX - ...and bit 5 or bit 3 (it lets what is inside be seen)
C 51340 If bit 5 of byte +5 of the record at IX is set, go back to #R$C873
C 51342 Test bit 3 of byte +5 of the record at IX
C 51346 If bit 3 of byte +5 of the record at IX is set, go back to #R$C873
C 51348 Swap AF with the shadow copy - Return the highest holder reached
C 51349 Restore IX from the stack
C 51351 Return to the caller
