c 52135 Refuse if the character is busy: 'SORRY, I CANNOT DO THAT NOW.'
D 52135 Called from both #R$E40A (SIT) and #R$E432 (GET OUT) before they do anything else. Checks bit 6 of a flag byte at #R$B934; if clear, returns immediately (continue normally). If set, discards the return address, prints a fixed message (#R$681A), and jumps to the shared failure point (#R$DC15) this project has seen several other entries use.
D 52135 Not yet confirmed: what sets bit 6 of #R$B934, and therefore what specific condition this guards against - a reasonable guess (already engaged in some other action, or otherwise unable to sit/stand right now) is just a guess, not tested. #R$B934/#R$B935 are the same bytes this project's #R$B91F investigation touched a few rounds earlier, not yet tied into a complete account.
D 52135 RESOLVED 2026-11-07: #R$B934 holds the first byte of the plan-script instruction the character was on when the player's request arrived (#R$B953; cleared each step at #R$CC89), and bit 6 of that byte marks the instruction as busy. Confirmed in the emulator: SAY TO WATSON "GET OUT" at the start gets 'Watson gets out of watsons armchair.'; with bit 6 poked into Watson's current instruction ($52 instead of $12) it gets 'Watson says " Sorry, I cannot do that now. "' and he stays in the chair.
