c 52551 Plan opcode 9, AWAIT: wait for a token from another actor
D 52551 Looks along the #R$9FE7 list for a node left by the actor named in the argument for this actor. Fails if there is none (scripts give AWAIT a failure address pointing at itself, so the actor waits); otherwise unlinks the node, frees it and succeeds. Confirmed in the emulator that AWAIT runs (3,909 of the 15,038 fetches were AWAITs, mostly Phipps at #R$EE2B waiting for Chief Constable Straker); the hand-over itself was not watched.
R 52551 Input:IX The instruction (+1 the actor the token must come from)
R 52551 Output:The step succeeds if the token was there (and is removed), otherwise it fails
