c 52671 Plan opcode 4, ASK: order another character to do something
D 52671 Verb #R$DD9E(46) (TALK TO) with the person as the direct object; queues an 8-byte node on the list at #R$9FEE (person, $FF, verb, dobj, iobj) and prints #R$682A, which quotes the order: the cabbie is told 'HAIL THE HANSOM CAB' this way, for example. The person carries the order out on its next turn (#R$CCA7). Read from the code; the message was rendered.
D 52671 Confirmed in the emulator: with the player moved to Inspector Lestrade at the start, his script hails a hansom cab, climbs in, and at 8:04 runs ASK (bytes 44 FA 1D FC FF: the person is the plan's remembered thing, here the cabbie; verb #R$9AF4(29) GO TO; the plan's indirect object, a room); #R$CE10 then prints 'Inspector Lestrade remarks to the cabbie " Go to Kings Cross Road. "'. (Rendered with 'you' as the actor, #R$682A reads 'YOU SAY TO ...'.)
