c 52920 A plan instruction failed: move on and try again now
D 52920 Counts the failure (#R$CC0B), skips the instruction and any success address, and takes the failure address if bit 4 is set. If that leads straight back to the same instruction the actor gives up for this turn (#R$CD8B); otherwise the next instruction is tried at once (#R$CC82).
D 52920 How it works:
D 52920 1. Count the failure in #R$CC0B.
D 52920 2. Skip the instruction and any success address. If the instruction has a failure address (bit 4), go there.
D 52920 3. If the new position is the same instruction, wait there until next turn (#R$CD8B); otherwise try the next one now.
