c 53724 Does this object list verb A in its own action list?
D 53724 IX = an entity record, A = a verb number. Skips the record's fixed part (15 bytes plus the n location bytes, n being byte 0) to reach its own action list: two-byte (verb, shared action index) pairs ended by $FF or $00. Returns carry set with IX on the matching pair, or carry clear if the verb is not listed.
D 53724 The end test is a compact trick: INC (IX) leaves zero only if the byte was $FF, and a following DEC (IX) restores it and leaves zero only if it was $00 - so one byte is tested for both terminators without loading it.
D 53724 Confirmed by reading all 110 entity records with this layout (objects.py): every door lists OPEN->6 and CLOSE->7, both armchairs list CLIMB OUT OF->8, CLIMB INTO->9, GET OUT OF->8, GET INTO->9, SIT IN->9, matching the live hits.
R 53724 Input:IX An entity record
R 53724 A A verb number
R 53724 Output:F Carry set with IX on the verb's pair if listed; carry clear if not
