c 53815 Resolve an id (in A) to its full entity record
D 53815 Looks the id up in the 3-byte index table at #R$8B6F (via #R$D34E above), which gives back a *pointer* to the entity's real, full record - one level of indirection past the compact index. Some register-juggling here (push/EX (SP),HL/pop) nets IX = that stored pointer on return; it looks unnecessarily roundabout on the page, but running it and checking IX directly confirms that's exactly what it does.
D 53815 Confirmed by calling this routine directly for ids 0-3 and dumping the records it resolves to: all four are 17 bytes long and laid out back-to-back in memory (0x8CBA, 0x8CCB, 0x8CDC, 0x8CED), all starting with the same tag byte ($01) that #R$D495 (below) checks for. See source/world_model_notes.md for the full record dumps and what's confirmed about their fields.
