c 54566 List the things in place A, then what each of them holds
D 54566 Names each listable thing (#R$D57D) with commas and a final AND (#R$D3D9, #R$A414), marking each as seen (+6 bit 7); then, for each that has things of its own to list (#R$D4CC), says how they are held (#R$D590) and lists those too (calling itself). Read from the code; it produces 'In watsons armchair there is Watson. Watson is carrying the daily chronicle.'
D 54566 How it works:
D 54566 1. First pass: name each listable thing in the place (#R$D57D), marking it as seen (+6 bit 7).
D 54566 2. After each name put a comma, but AND before the last two and a full stop after the last.
D 54566 3. Second pass: for each thing that holds others, say how it holds them (#R$D590) and list what it holds in the same way, going down the levels.
R 54566 Input:A A place
R 54566 C The number of things to name
R 54566 Output:The things named with commas and AND, each marked seen (+6 bit 7)
