c 54990 Read one word and classify it as noun or verb
D 54990 Calls the tokenizer (#R$D9C5) and checks its class-byte result: $D0 means noun (jumps to #R$D6E0 to handle that), $C0 means verb (falls through to accept it); anything else retries by calling the tokenizer again.
D 54990 Confirmed real by tracing a genuine word (TAKE) through this exact loop: three tokenizer calls happened in sequence, returning class bytes $30, then $B0 (the punctuation class this project found much earlier), then $C0 - accepted on the third attempt - with the OTHER half of the result (word index, held in E) staying fixed at 5 throughout all three. Read as: the tokenizer resolves the word immediately, but offers it under a sequence of candidate classes until one matches what the caller is looking for. Exactly why $30 and $B0 are tried first, before $C0, isn't confirmed.
