c 55290 Player's turn: turn the sentence into a command (RUN at $993C)
D 55290 Addresses named in the title: #R$993C.
D 55290 Part of the player's own script (see #R$993C): parses the sentence at #R$9FF2 into a verb and objects (#R$B191) and copies them into the plan registers (#R$9FD6-#R$9FD8), where the script's DO picks them up. With ALL (#R$A01A($A01C), kept in #R$D6B8 between turns) the sentence is kept so that the next turn takes the next thing; otherwise its node is freed, with any BUT nodes after it. If the sentence does not parse, an ALL that has run out of things fails quietly (#R$DC15, with #R$A032($A033) = $FF); anything else sets #R$D7E0 so that the rest of the line is thrown away (#R$D7E1). Read from the code.
D 55290 Tried 9 November: TAKE ALL (the 'ALL has run out' failure at #R$D865), TAKE ALL BUT LAMP (the BUT chain #R$D84F-#R$D856) and DROP ALL BUT LAMP both reached the paths that the stored routes do not. This record is one step of the loop in the player's own plan script at #R$9921: DO LOOK once, then read a line (#R$D6BF), split it into words (#R$D715), check there is a word (#R$D769), parse a sentence (#R$D77E), check there is a sentence (#R$D7D9), turn it into a command (#R$D7FA) and DO it. When you wear the china man's disguise the same script runs for him; the counts below include both.
D 55290 Seen in the emulator (9 November, tools/experiments/record_coverage.py over the 15 stored routes): the body ran 15,323 times in 14 of them, run by you, china man. Every one of its 53 instructions was executed (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py plus the targeted tests described above).
D 55290 How it works:
D 55290 1. Carry the ALL flag over from the last turn and take the sentence at #R$9FF2.
D 55290 2. Parse it into a verb and objects (#R$B191). If that fails, set the failure flag and finish.
D 55290 3. Put the verb and objects in the plan registers (#R$9FD6, #R$9FD7), and note where the ALL search got to.
D 55290 4. If ALL is still going keep the sentence; otherwise unhook and free its node.
R 55290 Input:$9FF2 The sentence
R 55290 Output:$9FD6 The verb
R 55290 $9FD7 The objects
R 55290 F Z if the sentence could not be made into a command
