c 55710 The '@' key on an empty line: do the last command again
D 55710 Reached from the line editor (#R$D8CF) when '@' is typed on an empty line. Unless a typed line still has sentences waiting (#R$A01A($A01B), when the key is ignored), sets #R$D714 and ends the input. The word-list builder at #R$D715 sees #R$D714 and, instead of tokenizing the line again, reuses the tokens already at #LINK(rom_symbols#a5B81)($5B81) - the previous command's. (#R$D9AC, shared with the time-out path, prints two backspaces.) Confirmed in the emulator: after NORTH into the closet, '@' gave 'YOU CANNOT GO NORTH.' twice.
