c 56167 Read an amount of pre-decimal money
D 56167 '£n' gives pounds; then 'nS' is shillings, 'nD' pence, and 'n/m' shillings and pence ('n/-' for none). The total is worked out in pence - (pounds x 20 + shillings) x 12 + pence - and packed into BC seven bits per byte with bit 7 of both bytes set, which is what tells a sum of money from a time (requirement code 6, PAY TO, wants bit 7 set in the low byte; code 5, WAIT UNTIL, wants it clear).
D 56167 Confirmed in the emulator (tools/experiments/money_test.py): '£1' reads as #R$81EF($81F0) (240 pence), '2/6' as #R$809A($809E) (30), '3S' as #R$80A2($80A4) (36), '1/-' as #R$808A($808C) (12), and '9:30AM' as #R$C91C($C91E); the game echoes them back as 'You pay £1 to Watson.', '2/6', '3/-' and '1/-'.
