c 56345 Action record: default for verb 35 (LOOK THROUGH)
D 56345 LOOK THROUGH <door>: after the pre-check at #R$DC6C, finds the exit through the door (#R$D46C); if it leads to a room (+2), moves the actor there for a moment (#R$DD0B), describes the room with 'YOU CAN SEE' instead of 'YOU ARE' (#R$D0DC = 1, #R$D1B2) and moves it back. Tried in the emulator 2026-11-08: LOOK THROUGH WINDOWS gets YOU CANNOT LOOK THROUGH THE WINDOW, LOOK THROUGH DOOR asks WHICH DOOR ?. The record's first seven bytes are header and arguments, not code.
D 56345 Tested 9 November (tools/experiments/untraced_tests.py, in the sitting room): LOOK THROUGH WINDOW gets 'YOU CANNOT LOOK THROUGH THE WINDOW', LOOK THROUGH YOUR DOOR with the door shut gets 'YOU CANNOT LOOK THROUGH YOUR DOOR', and after OPEN YOUR DOOR it prints 'You look through your door. You can see a hall.' - this is the only way found to run the body, so the door must be open. No stored route uses LOOK THROUGH.
D 56345 Every one of its 24 instructions was executed (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py plus the targeted tests described above).
