c 56407 Action record: default for verb 28 (GO THROUGH)
D 56407 GO THROUGH <door>. The characters use it constantly - Chief Constable Straker, the cook, the gardener, Lestrade, the local policeman, Phipps and others walk through doors with it - and the player can too (tested 9 November: with the door shut, GO THROUGH YOUR DOOR gets 'I SEE NO YOUR DOOR THAT YOU CAN GO THROUGH'; after OPEN YOUR DOOR it prints 'You go through your door.' and describes the hall). The verb becomes a GO in the door's direction. In the runs sampled the actor's room (+15) changed to the room on the other side of the door (Lestrade through the solid door, room 94 to 97; Straker through the large oak door, 63 to 64).
D 56407 Seen in the emulator (9 November, tools/experiments/record_coverage.py over the 15 stored routes): the body ran 6,834 times in 14 of them, run by cook, gardener, inspector lestrade, chief constable straker and others. Every one of its 16 instructions was executed (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py).
