c 56629 Can the actor get past the thing in an exit?
D 56629 Nothing in the way (A = 0) always lets the actor through. Otherwise the thing must be open - +5 bit 5, or bit 3 - and its size (+2) must be at least the actor's size (IY+2).
D 56629 This is how guards work: the local police men at Browns and Jones front gates are themselves the 'door' of the exit they stand in. They are 'open' (bit 5) with size 69, smaller than the player (96) and Watson (96), so neither can pass, while Lestrade (32) could. The hidden door into the opium den (85) and the front door between Camden Street and the entrance hall (32) are narrower than the player too. Confirmed by play: with the player's size poked down from 96 to 8, all five of those exits let the player through.
