D 56658 Decoded by tools/plan.py; see #R$CC78 for the language. Each sub-block is one instruction. Room and object numbers are as the game uses them (the reference pages list both). Labels for verbs 128-140 and for the common helper records (#R$E52F, #R$E57A, #R$E588, #R$E5A8, #R$DDBE, #R$F198) were read from those records' code, not tried one by one in the emulator.
D 56658 In an instruction, 'plan dobj' and 'plan iobj' are not fixed objects: they mean the direct and indirect object currently held in the actor's plan registers (bytes +4 and +5 of its actor record), so the same step works on whatever the actor is dealing with - for the player, the objects of the command just typed. 'plan verb' is the verb register (+3), 'self' is the acting character, and '-' means none.
