D 56673 The pre-check takes the direct object as a room number, finds the exit from the actor's room to it (#R$D471) and refuses if there is none or if the exit is not a plain movement direction (a value below 11); the body stores that direction in plan register #R$9FD7. Used by the walk-to-a-room sub-script at #R$DD52, which then DOes the direction. Seen: Watson, Lestrade and Straker walking between rooms - the register held, for example, 1 (north), 2 (south) or 4 (west).
D 56673 Seen in the emulator (9 November, tools/experiments/record_coverage.py over the 15 stored routes): the body ran 2,887 times in 14 of them, run by watson, chief constable straker, inspector lestrade, major percival ffoulkes. Every one of its 13 instructions was executed (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py).
