c 56989 Shared OPEN action ($AA71 entry #6, CLOSE is #7)
D 56989 Addresses named in the title: #R$AA71.
D 56989 Confirmed real by breakpointing #R$C960 (the #R$AA71 table lookup) during a real `OPEN PLAIN DOOR` and seeing it reliably look up index 6 - this address - not as a static coincidence but as a repeated, live hit during real command execution.
D 56989 OPEN: `LD IX,(#R$A012($A013)); SET 5,(IX+5)` - sets bit 5 of the target record's field +5. CLOSE is the next record, #R$AA71 entry #7 at #R$DEAF (an earlier version of this entry wrongly called it a 'sub-entry' of #6): the same, but `RES 5,(IX+5)`. This confirms bit 5 of field +5 means 'is this thing open' - which also explains a flag the containment-chain walker (#R$C86E) was found checking several rounds earlier, without knowing what it meant.
D 56989 The chunk after CLOSE (#R$DEC1) is not part of this entry: it is the default action record for PUT IN / PUT ON / DROP IN (verbs #R$DEC1(38), #R$DEC1(39) and #R$DEC1(17), via the #R$9F38 table) - see overlay_04_actions.py.
D 56989 This is one entry in what's best understood as a small library of shared, generic action implementations that individual objects' own compact records can reference (rather than every openable object needing its own custom OPEN code) - see source/world_model_notes.md for how this reframes #R$AA71 as a whole, correcting the earlier 'verb dispatch table' guess.
