b 57898 A table searched by $E207 (part of TELL)
D 57898 Addresses named in the title: #R$E207.
D 57898 Decoded 9 November. The table is a list of groups, one per person: the person's id, then pairs of (topic id, message address) until $FF. The loop at #R$E207 finds the person, then #R$E201 finds the topic in that group; the message is printed through #R$6830 as the person's reply. A group that starts with $FE matches any person (the fallback), and a second $FF ends the table. Topic ids are things: $10 what happened, $11 your alibi, $12 your address, $0F the case, $43 the bloodstained clothes, and the people $05 Strachan, $06 Phipps, $07 the Major, $0D Tricia Fender.
D 57898 Gardener ($08): what happened and alibi share one reply (a gun shot woke him, he found Mrs Brown), and the Major gets another ('such a nice fellow... fighting'). Cook ($09): what happened/alibi (one reply), Phipps (overheard Basil and Daphne arguing about the will). Maid ($0A): what happened/alibi (Basil must have something to do with it). Phipps ($06): what happened/alibi (playing Chopin), address (Camden Street in London, Cobden Lane at Leatherhead). Strachan ($05): what happened/alibi (knows nothing), Tricia (she was Mr Brown's secretary), the Major (a friend of Mrs Jones). Straker ($04): the case (#R$7371, his report). The Major ($07): alibi (not at liberty to say; in London), address (Sidmouth Street). Tricia ($0D) and Mrs Jones ($5F): the bloodstained clothes (the confession 'you found out, I am really Mrs Jones'); Mrs Jones also gives the confession for what happened/alibi and a short reply about Tricia ('blackmailing Mrs Brown'). The $FE fallback answers your address, what happened and your alibi with 'DON'T BE SILLY.' (#R$6845). Message texts rendered with the game's own printer (source/render_messages.py).
