c 58746 Script helper: tick the countdown (fail when it runs out)
D 58746 Its pre-check (#R$E573) refuses when the actor has no countdown. The body counts it down: still running, the instruction succeeds - taking no time, so the script goes straight on (scripts pair it with IDLE, #R$E5A8, which takes a minute); at zero the countdown is removed and the instruction fails, so a script can 'do X until the time is up' with a success branch back to X. Read from the code.
