c 59150 Action record: the cabbie's parting shout (RUN at $F35C)
D 59150 Addresses named in the title: #R$F35C.
D 59150 The cabbie's parting shout when a passenger has gone without paying: 'The cabbie shouts " You bloody snob, watch out if we ever meet again ... "' (#R$6C54). Seen in end4b, after Major Percival Ffoulkes climbed out of the cab unpaid ('What about me money guv'nor?' repeated first). The record reads +3 of the actor's table record (the saved direct-object register, #R$CFB6): if it is non-zero it prints the shout; if it is zero it sets the ROM variable #LINK(rom_symbols#a5C3C)($5C3C) to 1 first and then prints (what that does to the print was not tested; #R$E720 and #R$E722 never ran). When I climbed out unpaid myself in a test the cabbie only repeated 'What about me money guv'nor?' for the next seven hours, so the route to the shout is not simply 'leave without paying'.
D 59150 Seen in the emulator (9 November, tools/experiments/record_coverage.py over the 15 stored routes): the body ran 46 times in 12 of them, run by cabbie. 12 of its 14 instructions were executed; the rest (#R$E720 #R$E722) never ran in any stored route, and were therefore read from the code only.
R 59150 Output:F NZ; the cabbie's shout printed, if the player can see it
