D 59367 Decoded by tools/plan.py; see #R$CC78 for the language. Each sub-block is one instruction. Room and object numbers are as the game uses them (the reference pages list both). Labels for verbs 128-140 and for the common helper records (#R$E52F, #R$E57A, #R$E588, #R$E5A8, #R$DDBE, #R$F198) were read from those records' code, not tried one by one in the emulator.
D 59367 In an instruction, 'plan dobj' and 'plan iobj' are not fixed objects: they mean the direct and indirect object currently held in the actor's plan registers (bytes +4 and +5 of its actor record), so the same step works on whatever the actor is dealing with - for the player, the objects of the command just typed. 'plan verb' is the verb register (+3), 'self' is the acting character, and '-' means none.
D 59367 The endgame (#R$EA25-#R$EAF3($EAF5)). Once PHIPPS HAS PLANS is proven (#R$EB19) he keeps asking 'HAVE YOU FOUND WHERE THE SALE LOCATION IS.' whenever you are with him. As soon as THE SALE LOCATION IS OLD MILL ROAD is proven too (#R$EB11) he sets off (#R$EA5B) - with or without you: he signals Chief Constable Straker, travels to Leatherhead (#R$EB72), climbs into the police cab (#R$EA69) and has the constable drive to Old Mill Road. There, if you are not in the cab with him (#R$EA78) he gives up and goes home (#R$EA84). If you are, and Phipps is still there (#R$EA7E), they drive back to Main Street and walk north to platform two at Leatherhead (room 55), and he says 'I AM AFRAID THAT BASIL HAS ELUDED US HOLMES.'. Left alone he waits there for a train and goes home on it (#R$EAD0, then #R$EA95 and #R$EB28: platform four, Kings Cross Road, a cab to Parliament Street). But that waiting loop is the one stretch of this part of his script without the busy flag, so he takes orders there; and once off platform two with no train in, his script follows you (verb #R$EB8B(134), #R$EAE2) until you reach platform one at Victoria (room 30) - where Phipps is heading, and where Lestrade has to be for the winning ending (#R$9E48). Confirmed in the emulator (tools/experiments/lestrade_follow.py): on platform two with his script at #R$EAD0, SAY TO LESTRADE "FOLLOW ME" and he followed every step south to Main Street and beyond (carrying out the order - his script position moved to the order's own sub-script, #R$E482 then #R$DD5F). Either way, if he gets back to Scotland Yard he says that Basil has eluded you, and ends the game with the papers at 10am (#R$EAB3).
D 59367 Logged in the emulator with both statements poked proven (tools/experiments/lestrade_route.py): he set off from Parliament Street at 7:05am on Wednesday and reached Old Mill Road at 10:45am, before Phipps; started at 11am instead (tools/experiments/win_test.py) he arrived at 3:13pm.
D 59367 The chase, played in the emulator (tools/experiments/chase.py, from 11am on Wednesday with the statements poked proven and you put in Leatherhead's Main Street as Lestrade arrives). The police cab holds only so much: climb in too early and you and Watson fill it, so Lestrade is left behind and the cab drives off without him; too late and Lestrade and Chief Constable Straker fill it ('I SEE NO POLICE CAB THAT YOU CAN CLIMB INTO'); in the minute Lestrade climbs in, you, Watson and Lestrade fit and Straker stays out. Then: Old Mill Road at 3:13pm, 'As you enter Basil Phipps whips his horses into action...' at 3:14, back in Main Street at 4:47, and Phipps walks to platform two and boards the train at 4:54. It leaves at 4:55 - one minute before Lestrade, still saying that Basil has eluded you, will take an order. Told to follow, he and Watson came on the next train (6:18), which reached platform four at 7:30; Phipps had left the game by 6:45 (between 6:30 and 6:45 in the logs), having found nobody at Victoria. Asking the constable to drive the police cab to Buckingham Palace Road did nothing; asked for Kings Cross Road - one of its three routes (#R$9AA3) - it went, with Lestrade and Watson aboard, but took 95 minutes and arrived at 6:42, just as Phipps walked onto platform one at Victoria. The trains run every 90 minutes (#R$F278), so missing the 4:55 costs an hour and a half. The plain GO TO and the train both lose; the furious police cab and the underground train win - see below.
D 59367 The winning line, played in the emulator (tools/experiments/chase.py stages A B C D E F2 G3). The case statements were poked proven and you and Watson were put in Leatherhead's Main Street at about 1:33 on Wednesday, as Lestrade reached the station with the police cab waiting for him; everything after that was typed: (1) CLIMB INTO POLICE CAB in the minute Lestrade climbs in, so that you, Watson and he fit and Straker stays out; (2) Old Mill Road at 3:13pm, and Phipps bolts at 3:14; (3) the police cab is back in Main Street at 4:47 - CLIMB OUT, NORTH three times, and at 4:56 on platform two, where his script stops being busy, SAY TO LESTRADE "FOLLOW ME"; (4) SOUTH three times, CLIMB INTO POLICE CAB (Lestrade and Watson follow), SAY TO POLICE MAN "GO FURIOUSLY TO KINGS CROSS ROAD" - verb #R$9ACB(30), which the constable's action list sends to the 20-minutes-quicker record (#R$9ACB): Kings Cross Road at 6:22; (5) CLIMB OUT, NORTHEAST twice to platform one, CLIMB INTO TRAIN at 6:28 - the underground train that runs Kings Cross, Paddington, Victoria (actors 36-41, #R$F21D); (6) platform one at Victoria at 6:40, where a German agent is waiting; (7) at 6:42 'Basil Phipps enters.' and 'As Basil enters he sees you and pulls a gun. With suprising agility Watson pushes you out of the way of Basils first shot allowing Lestrade time to pull his gun and capture the culprits. As incredible as it may seem you have solved this case. You truly deserve the title of worlds greatest detective.' Two minutes to spare. The hansom cabs are no use for the last leg: at 6:22 both are already on the road, cab 30 carrying Phipps and cab 33 the German agent (their containers, logged), a minute apart. Played again with less help (stages A B2 C2 D E F2 G3): from Holmes's rooms at 11am on Wednesday, with only the statements poked proven, #R$9D90 and #R$9E87($9E88) poked - the marks a player earns by meeting Lestrade with Straker on Monday and by proving the Major's statement, without which the game ends early (at 3pm on Monday, or about 1am on Tuesday) - and Watson put beside you on his follow loop (in stage A you never left your room, so his own script had gone idle) - OPEN YOUR DOOR, WEST, DOWN, OPEN FRONT DOOR, SOUTH, HAIL CAB, CLIMB INTO HANSOM CAB, SAY TO CABBIE "GO TO KINGS CROSS ROAD", NORTHEAST four times to platform three, the 12:25 to Leatherhead, SOUTH twice to Main Street (1:36, with Lestrade), CLIMB INTO POLICE CAB when his script reaches #R$EA69, and the rest as above: won again at 6:42.
D 59367 UPDATE, 9 November: the winning line described above, and every other ending named in this block, has since been reached by typed commands only, from a fresh boot, with nothing poked (tools/experiments/playthrough/v12_clean_win.cmds and endings/*.cmds). The order that matters on Wednesday: THE SALE LOCATION IS OLD MILL ROAD said at 10:53am; hansom cab (not Lestrade's) to Kings Cross Road; noon train; out at platform one; police cab at 1:37pm in the minute Lestrade boards; at 4:56pm on platform two SAY TO LESTRADE "FOLLOW ME" once; police cab GO FURIOUSLY TO KINGS CROSS ROAD (74 minutes); the 6:29 train from Kings Cross platform one, boarded in the minute it is in, so that Lestrade (who follows a turn behind) is aboard; Victoria platform one at 6:41.
D 59367 Played, 9 November (tools/experiments/playthrough/endings/end6_* and end7_*): left alone on platform two at 4:55pm Lestrade says 'has eluded us Holmes' at 4:56 and takes the 6:15pm train (script #R$EBF1), reaches platform four at 7:31, Kings Cross Road at 7:41, a hansom cab at 7:46, Parliament Street at 8:01 and Scotland Yard at 8:06pm (script #R$EA99, which then waits for 10pm; #R$EAAD puts him off stage at 10:01pm). The speech is only printed if you are in the room: riding the same train and cab and walking EAST into Scotland Yard at 8:02pm, you hear 'I am afraid that Basil has eluded us Holmes.' at 8:04pm. At Thursday 10:00am the script is at #R$EAB3 and the papers ending fires (end7_eluded_at_scotland_yard). Observed, not just read from the code.
