c 61340 Action record: the first messenger takes a note from Basil (RUN at $EE95)
D 61340 Addresses named in the title: #R$EE95.
D 61340 Prints 'A messenger arrives at the door, takes a note from Basil and dissapears down the street.' (#R$75E8). It is run by Phipps's script at #R$EE95 on Tuesday at 1pm, only when you (or the china man) are in Camden Street or Basil's front yard (rooms 32 and 102). No stored route is there at that hour, so I tested it on 9 November (tools/experiments/untraced_tests.py, part E): I replayed the winning route to Tuesday 12:30pm in Kings Cross Road, moved the player to Camden Street by writing the room number into memory (the only poke in this pass) and typed WAIT: at about 1:00pm the message was printed. Its sibling at #R$EFAC (Wednesday 9:50am) ran in the stored routes.
D 61340 Every one of its 6 instructions was executed (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py plus the targeted tests described above).
R 61340 Output:F NZ; the message printed
B 61340,2 Action record header: flags $00; byte 1 $00
C 61342 Point HL at the message text, "A messenger arrives at the door, takes a note from Basil and disappears down the street." (#R$75E8)
C 61345 A = 1: the value the output switch needs for the message to appear on screen. (A second entry point: the sibling record at #R$EFAC joins here with its own HL.)
C 61347 Store it in the output-switch byte (#LINK(rom_symbols#a5C3C)($5C3C)), so the print routine really draws the text instead of staying silent
C 61350 Print the message at HL (#R$A59F)
C 61353 OR $01 makes A non-zero, which clears the zero flag: the plan interpreter reads "not zero" as "the action happened"
C 61355 Return to the plan interpreter
c 61356 Action record: the second messenger gives a note to Basil (RUN at $EF01)
D 61356 Addresses named in the title: #R$EF01.
D 61356 Prints 'A messenger arrives at the door, gives a note to Basil and dissapears down the street.' (#R$7603), with the same output switch setting as #R$EF9C. Run by Phipps's script at #R$EF01 on Wednesday morning when you or the china man are outside, which is why it appears in the winning route.
D 61356 Seen in the emulator (9 November, tools/experiments/record_coverage.py over the 15 stored routes): the body ran 7 times in 7 of them, run by phipps. Every one of its 2 instructions was executed (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py).
R 61356 Output:F NZ; the message printed
B 61356,2 Action record header: flags $00; byte 1 $00
C 61358 Point HL at the message "A MESSENGER ARRIVES AT THE DOOR, GIVES A NOTE TO... (#R$7603)
C 61361 Go back to #R$EFA1
c 61363 Action record: Phipps goes to sleep (RUN at $EE3D, $EEBB)
D 61363 Addresses named in the title: #R$EE3D, #R$EEBB.
D 61363 Sets the actor's state word to SLEEPING ($07F0), the high nibble of +8 to 1, and clears bit 6 of +5 (not a person any more), through #R$F1C1. Seen: thing 6 (Phipps) +9/+10 went from 0 to $07F0, +8 from $86 to $16 and +5 from $E0 to $A0.
D 61363 Seen in the emulator (9 November, tools/experiments/record_coverage.py over the 15 stored routes): the body ran 22 times in 12 of them, run by phipps. Every one of its 7 instructions was executed (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py).
R 61363 Input:$A036 The actor
R 61363 Output:F NZ; the actor asleep, no longer a person to talk to
B 61363,2 Action record header: flags $00; byte 1 $00
C 61365 Load DE with $07F0 - DE = $07F0, B = $10
C 61368 Load B with $10
C 61370 Read #R$A032($A036) in "Game variables" into A - The actor's record (#R$F1C1)
C 61373 Call the routine "Set a thing's state word and state bits" (#R$F1C1)
C 61376 Clear bit 6 of +5
C 61380 Make A non-zero, which clears the zero flag, and hand that back to the caller - Return NZ
C 61382 Return to the caller
c 61383 Action record: Phipps wakes at 7 - or shoots you if you are in the house (RUN at $EE46, $EEC3, $EEDB, $EF09)
D 61383 Addresses named in the title: #R$EE46, #R$EEC3, #R$EEDB, #R$EF09.
D 61383 If the player is in one of the rooms of Basil's house (33 to 39, the seven compares at #R$EFC9-#R$EFE4) control goes to #R$DFCC and Basil shoots you; otherwise the state word is cleared, the high nibble of +8 becomes 8 and bit 6 of +5 is set again - he is awake and a person again. Seen: thing 6 +9/+10 went from $07F0 to 0, +8 from $16 to $86 and +5 from $A0 to $E0 (11 sampled runs); with you in the house the branch to #R$DFCC ran twice in the stored routes.
D 61383 Seen in the emulator (9 November, tools/experiments/record_coverage.py over the 15 stored routes): the body ran 5,592 times in 11 of them, run by phipps. Every one of its 20 instructions was executed (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py).
R 61383 Input:$A009 The player's room
R 61383 Output:F NZ; Phipps wakes, or shoots the player if the player is in Basil's house
B 61383,2 Action record header: flags $00; byte 1 $00
C 61385 Read the room the player is in, which decides what is shown (#R$A002($A009)) into A - The player's room (#R$A002($A009)): one of Basil's house (33 entrance hall to 39 yard; the seven compares run $23, $21, $22, $26, $25, $24, $27)?
C 61388 Compare A with $23
C 61390 If A equals $23, skip ahead to #R$EFE6
C 61392 Compare A with $21
C 61394 If A equals $21, skip ahead to #R$EFE6
C 61396 Compare A with $22
C 61398 If A equals $22, skip ahead to #R$EFE6
C 61400 Compare A with $26
C 61402 If A equals $26, skip ahead to #R$EFE6
C 61404 Compare A with $25
C 61406 If A equals $25, skip ahead to #R$EFE6
C 61408 Compare A with $24
C 61410 If A equals $24, skip ahead to #R$EFE6
C 61412 Compare A with $27
C 61414 Yes: take the other branch at #R$DFCC
C 61417 Load DE with $0000 - No: DE = 0, B = $80, and clear then re-set bit 6 of the record's +5 (#R$EFBA)...
C 61420 Load B with $80
C 61422 Call #R$EFBA (inside "Action record: Phipps goes to sleep (RUN at...")
