c 61699 The Major's confession: establish 'MAJOR VISITED OPIUM DEN'
D 61699 Run by the Major's script (#R$F0E6) right after he tells the player 'WELL HOLMES YOU HAVE FOUND OUT MY SHAMEFUL SECRET, I AM ADDICTED TO...' - which he only does when the player is with him in the opium den late at night (his script: after 11pm, by chance, to room 40 and through the heavy oak door). Marks the empty evidence record at #R$996F done, which is the only way to prove MAJOR PERCIVAL FFOULKES VISITED OPIUM DEN and so MAJOR PERCIVAL FFOULKES IS INNOCENT. Confirmed in the emulator (tools/experiments/major_test.py): with the player moved to Lestrade at the start, MAJOR FFOULKES IS INNOCENT is marked waiting ($A4 -> $A5) and Lestrade at once asks 'Well can you prove that Major Percival Ffoulkes is innocent yet, Holmes ?'; MAJOR FFOULKES VISITED THE OPIUM DEN gets 'I do not believe that you have the evidence...'. With bit 1 of #R$996F($9972) set first - as #R$F103 does when the Major confesses - the opium-den statement is proven, the waiting innocence statement is proven with it (#R$9965($9968) $A5 -> $A6), #R$9A3D sets #R$9E87($9E88) and Lestrade says 'Very good Holmes, I shall return to Leather head tomorrow to have another look around.'
R 61699 Output:F NZ; the statement at $996F is established
B 61699,2 Action record header: flags $00; byte 1 $00
C 61701 Point IX at #R$996F in "The case: statements about the crime, and..." - Case record #R$996F (Major Ffoulkes visited the opium den): bit 1 of +3 set - the statement is established
C 61705 Set bit 1 of byte +3 of the record at IX
C 61709 Make A non-zero, which clears the zero flag, and hand that back to the caller - Succeed
C 61711 Return to the caller
