D 62606 Two flags used by the fill (#R$F490) to remember whether the rows above and below have been seeded.
c 62608 Fill the area around the pen in colour A
D 62608 A scan-line flood fill: the colour goes to #R$F60B, seeds are kept on the stack (a $00B0 marker ends them), and each row is filled left and right, seeding the rows above and below (#R$F48E/#R$F48E($F48F)). Read from the code; the drawn pictures show it works.
D 62608 How it works:
D 62608 1. Keep the colour at #R$F60B and put a marker on the stack.
D 62608 2. From the seed, go left until the pixel is set or the edge is reached, colouring as it goes.
D 62608 3. Work along the lines above and below: the first clear pixel of each run of clear pixels is pushed as a seed for later.
D 62608 4. Pop seeds and repeat until the marker is reached.
R 62608 Input:A The colour
R 62608 DE The seed point
R 62608 Output:The area around the seed filled; DE, HL kept
