c 62740 Move attribute address HL up a row (not past the top)
D 62740 #R$F525 down, #R$F536 left, #R$F540 right: the four moves of a colour run (bit 5 commands in #R$F3C2).
D 62740 How it works:
D 62740 1. Each of the four entry points moves HL, the address of an attribute byte, one cell: #R$F514 up a row, #R$F525 down a row, #R$F536 left and #R$F540 right.
D 62740 2. A row is 32 bytes. After the move the high byte is checked against the edges of the attribute area (#LINK(rom_symbols#a5800)($5800) to $59FF): if the move left it, it is undone, so the address never leaves the screen.
R 62740 Input:HL An attribute address
R 62740 Output:HL The address one cell on, or unchanged at the edge
R 62740 AF is preserved
C 62740 Save AF on the stack - HL 32 bytes back, unless that leaves the attribute area
